## Verdict

Revise. Spec prereview of `studio/briefs/W-110.md` revision 1, advisory (the
spec gate is the architect's; this is the Censor's first hour, QA lex §1).
4 MUST, 8 SHOULD. The brief is unusually well grounded — twenty-odd measured
rows reproduce verbatim, and the three design choices the Patron's charter
would otherwise own (no digest in the manifest, no `^` anchor on a playwright
grep, seeding rather than changing a route) are each supported by a probe I
re-ran. What blocks it is narrower: the manifest validator's clause ordering
is unspecified while three behaviour rows assert exact finding counts that
depend on it, the rule's read loop is unbounded, one stated pipeline
guarantee is about the wrong stream, and the forced edit to the existing ui
fixtures is specified against a helper signature that cannot carry what the
new header needs.

